export const guides=[JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(new URL('./nov13-brazil-draft.json',import.meta.url),'utf8')),
{file:'uae-wpc-wall-panels-tender-addendum-requotation.html',image:'november13-uae.webp',product:'/products/wpc-wall-panels.html',catalog:'/assets/catalogs/3d-pvc-panel-catalog.pdf',source:'https://www.iso.org/files/live/sites/isoorg/files/standards/docs/en/iso_9001_2015_guidance_documented_information.pdf',sourceName:'ISO: guidance on documented information',related:['uzbekistan-wpc-wall-panels-order-revision-control.html'],en:{title:'UAE WPC Panels: Requote a Tender Addendum | Luvie',heading:'UAE WPC wall panels: turn a tender addendum into a comparable revised quotation',description:'Compare WPC specification, finish and quantity changes before accepting a revised quotation for an interior project in the UAE.',lead:'A tender update can change much more than the total area of WPC wall panels. A revised elevation may introduce a different profile, add returns around openings or replace a finish in only part of the project. If a buyer forwards the new drawing without identifying the changes, competing quotations may price different scopes. For a UAE interior procurement package, the useful output is a reconciled change schedule that lets the buyer compare the earlier quotation with the new one. This is a purchasing workflow, not a statement of local tender law.',answer:'Issue one identified addendum package with a line-by-line list of added, removed and changed requirements. Ask the supplier to acknowledge the exact revision and show the commercial effect separately from unchanged items. Do not accept a revised grand total until the model, finish, quantity units, accessories and exclusions have been reconciled.',sections:[['Start with the priced baseline','Identify the quotation number and the drawing, specification and quantity schedule on which it was based. Record the actual WPC profile reference, finish reference and proposed length rather than a broad description such as wood-look wall panel. Confirm whether quantities were stated as panels, packs or area and how any conversion was calculated. Keep this baseline available throughout the comparison. Without it, a new quote may look cheaper simply because one party has omitted trims or priced a different quantity basis. The baseline is a reference for comparison, not automatic permission to order a superseded configuration. Mark it accordingly so the site or purchasing team does not mistake the comparison copy for the current release.'],['Describe each changed requirement','Build a change table with the original requirement, revised requirement, affected room or elevation and controlling document reference. Separate a new finish from a new profile; similar photographs do not establish that the same tooling, dimensions or accessory arrangement is proposed. If an area increases, identify whether the new area uses an existing reference or introduces another combination. Ask the responsible design team to resolve unclear transitions and exposed edges before the supplier assumes a detail. ISO guidance on documented information provides a general basis for keeping process information usable and controlled. It does not certify Luvie or prescribe a UAE tender procedure. The change table here is a practical recommendation tailored to this procurement problem.'],['Request a quote that exposes the differences','Ask for the revised quantities and units alongside the corresponding product references. Identify additions, deletions and unchanged lines separately; a supplier may reasonably need to reassess packing or other commercial terms, but those effects should be explicit. Confirm whether existing accessories remain appropriate when the panel configuration changes. Request a clear statement of exclusions and unresolved assumptions rather than accepting a blanket note that the price is subject to drawings. Compare currency, commercial basis and the scope of any delivery allowance consistently. This guide does not provide a price, lead time or minimum order. Obtain those terms from the actual quotation and avoid interpreting a previous offer as a current commitment.'],['Close the addendum before ordering','Record the supplier acknowledgement of the issued revision and obtain internal approval of the reconciled scope. Acknowledging receipt alone does not confirm that every change has been priced. Resolve exceptions in writing and link the final quotation to the accepted addendum package. Before releasing the purchase order, check the panel references, finish allocation, quantities and accessory lines against that accepted version. Archive earlier comparisons without deleting their history, while making the current purchase basis easy to identify. If another revision arrives, reopen only the affected comparison with an explicit decision on the remaining scope. This prevents a running conversation from becoming an accidental mixture of several tender versions.']],checklist:['Identify the original priced document set.','Separate profile, finish, quantity and accessory changes.','Obtain line-level revised scope and explicit exclusions.','Link the accepted quotation and purchase order to the same addendum.'],faq:[['Is a supplier email saying received enough?','It establishes receipt, not complete pricing acceptance. Ask the supplier to identify included changes and any exceptions before the buyer approves the revised offer.'],['Can we compare only the new total?','That can conceal changed quantities or exclusions. Reconcile the product and commercial scope first, then compare the totals on the same basis.']],closing:'Send Luvie the WPC references, revised finish allocation and an annotated change schedule. Request a quotation tied to that revision, with unresolved assumptions shown separately.'}},
{file:'uzbekistan-pu-stone-panels-purchaser-transition-open-orders.html',image:'november13-uzbekistan.webp',product:'/products/pu-stone-panels.html',catalog:'/assets/catalogs/pu-stone-panel-catalog.pdf',source:'https://www.iso.org/files/live/sites/isoorg/files/archive/pdf/en/documented_information.pdf',sourceName:'ISO: documented information guidance',related:['uzbekistan-pu-stone-panels-showroom-branch-handover.html'],en:{title:'Uzbekistan PU Panels: Hand Over Open Orders | Luvie',heading:'Uzbekistan PU stone panels: hand over open orders when the purchasing contact changes',description:'Preserve PU model, mould texture, approved sample and outstanding order decisions when a new buyer takes responsibility for an Uzbekistan project.',lead:'A new purchasing contact may inherit an inbox full of PU stone-panel photographs but no clear record of which texture was approved or what remains to be delivered. A similar-looking sample can then be mistaken for the ordered model, while unresolved finish questions disappear into an old chat. For an Uzbekistan importer or project buyer, the handover should preserve the identity and current decision status of each open order. This differs from transferring spare stock or moving a showroom display: the aim is to let a new buyer continue an unfinished transaction without silently changing its basis.',answer:'Create an open-order handover that connects each purchase line to its confirmed model, texture reference, finish and approved sample. Reconcile ordered, delivered and outstanding quantities, list unresolved decisions with owners, and obtain acknowledgement from the incoming buyer and established supplier contact. A change of contact does not itself authorize a product substitution.',sections:[['Recover the exact product identity','Start with the accepted purchase document rather than the latest attractive photograph. Record the PU model reference, stated dimensions and finish identification from that document. Where mould or texture references are available, include them explicitly and distinguish them from a commercial color name. Link the approved sample identifier and its acceptance record; a photograph without a reference may be useful context but is not enough to prove equivalence. If two records disagree, flag the conflict for confirmation before the incoming buyer places a repeat order. Do not invent missing model details from appearance. The handover should make uncertainty visible instead of making an incomplete file look complete.'],['Reconcile every open quantity','For each line, show the ordered quantity, documented receipts, any accepted changes and the balance still requiring action. Keep the units consistent and explain a conversion between panels and cartons using confirmed packing information. Separate a physically received quantity from one merely described as dispatched, and separate commercial acceptance from a transport update. List any held, rejected or disputed items without assuming the outcome of the claim. Link supporting records so the incoming buyer can reconstruct the balance. A spreadsheet total that cannot be traced to the source documents is not a reliable starting point for a replacement order or final delivery instruction.'],['Transfer decisions as well as documents','List pending sample approvals, finish clarifications, document requests and other open actions with the responsible person and the next required response. Include the latest agreed answer, not only the question that started the conversation. Identify who may approve changes under the buyer’s actual procedures; a newly copied colleague should not be treated as an authorized approver by assumption. ISO guidance recognizes the importance of documented information for operating and controlling processes. The handover proposed here is an application of that general idea, not a claim of certification or an Uzbekistan-specific legal requirement. Keep commercially sensitive records in the approved business system rather than attaching everything to a public inquiry.'],['Confirm the handover without changing the order','Arrange an acknowledgement that the incoming contact has received the current order basis and outstanding action list. Ask the established supplier contact to confirm the relevant commercial references and the correct route for subsequent questions. Keep any bank-detail change outside this routine product handover and subject to independent finance verification. If the incoming buyer wants a different texture or finish, initiate a separate documented change instead of editing the inherited reference. Retain the earlier correspondence as history while clearly identifying the current action owner. A successful handover ends with the next decision being obvious, not with an unsupported declaration that all open orders are complete.']],checklist:['Tie each line to the accepted PU model and sample reference.','Reconcile delivered and outstanding quantities in confirmed units.','Assign an owner and next action to every unresolved decision.','Acknowledge the new contact without implying a product substitution.'],faq:[['Can the new buyer approve a similar texture from a photograph?','A photograph can support discussion, but the proposed reference and the approval basis must be confirmed. Do not treat visual similarity as proof that the ordered model is unchanged.'],['Does a change of purchasing contact require a new order?','Not automatically. Follow the actual contract and internal procedures. Preserve the existing order basis, then document any genuine scope change separately.']],closing:'Send Luvie the PU order and model references, approved sample identifier and outstanding questions. Ask for a reference-by-reference confirmation so the incoming buyer can continue the correct transaction.'}}
];
